schema: "0.4"
id: npl-nocturne-41-mock-mcp-llm-pool
type: image
quality: high

# NoizuPromptLingo (a prompt-definition language + MCP toolchain for agent engineers) — Mock MCP LLM Pool settings screen.
# Theme tenets: dark-native near-black canvas, single phosphor-green "live" signal, mono-first, 4px radius, flat surface-step elevation (no glow/gradient).
# Palette: canvas #010409, panel #0d1117, raised #161b22, text #e6edf3, secondary #909dab, signal green #3fb950, link cyan #58a6ff, amber #d29922.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    dark-native agent-engineering instrument — a settings surface for the pool of
    LLMs that power mock MCP servers. Cool terminal dark throughout; the ONLY
    saturated color is a single phosphor-green "live"/enabled signal. Monospace is
    a co-equal voice (model names, IDs render mono). Flat surfaces separated by
    lightness steps, never drop shadows or glow.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of the Mock MCP · LLM Pool settings screen of
    NoizuPromptLingo — managing the pool of models available to power mock MCP
    servers' simulated tool responses.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (two bands): a slim LEFT NAV RAIL on the darkest near-black
    canvas ("the rack", one active settings item marked by a 2px phosphor-green
    left rail), and a CONTENT AREA on a lighter dark panel.

    SETTINGS HEADER (top of content): a breadcrumb-style eyebrow "Mock MCP · LLM
    Pool" in mono, a title "LLM Pool" in off-white sans, a muted one-line
    description, and a right-aligned primary ADD MODEL TO POOL button — a solid
    phosphor-green fill with near-black label, 4px radius, the one lit control.

    DEFAULT MODEL SELECTOR (a compact card above the table): a labeled row
    "Default model for new mock servers" with a selector pill showing a mono model
    name and a chevron; quiet dark border, recessed field feel.

    LLM POOL TABLE (dominant): a dense settings table, quiet dark hairline row
    separators, a faint raised header row "Model · Provider · Context · Enabled".
    ~7 rows, each: a mono MODEL NAME (e.g. a versioned model id), a muted provider
    label, a mono context-window value, and an ENABLED TOGGLE on the right — the ON
    toggles filled phosphor-green with the knob to the right, the OFF toggles a
    muted dark ghost. One or two rows off; most on.

    PALETTE & TYPE: cool near-black canvas, a lighter dark panel, soft off-white
    text, cool grey secondary; phosphor-green reserved for the Add button, the
    active nav rail, and the ON toggles — green means enabled/live. Inter for UI;
    JetBrains Mono for model names, context values, and ids — mono prominent.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: 4px radius on the button, selector, and card; flat fills,
    elevation by surface-lightness steps; low dark borders, recessed selector. No
    gradients, no glow, no scanlines.

    MOOD: focused, administrative, instrument-like — a quiet dark settings surface
    where green marks what is switched on.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, neon glow, bloom, CRT scanlines, gradient background, pure-black OLED background, pure-white surfaces"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches Mock MCP LLM Pool: nav rail, settings header with Add Model to Pool, a default-model selector, and an LLM pool table with model/provider/context columns and per-row enabled toggles"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Dark-native canvas, single phosphor-green signal on the Add button + ON toggles, mono model names/ids, 4px radius, flat surface-step elevation, recessed fields, no glow/gradient"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear settings hierarchy, plausible table-driven layout, comfortable density"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "neon glow, bloom, or gradient wash (breaks the flat dark instrument register)"

tags: [npl-nocturne, NoizuPromptLingo, screen-mockup]
